{% set local_problem %}
<p>Albertville's tree mix keeps gutters busy. Pine needles accumulate year-round — they're small enough to mat together and block water flow even when gutters don't look "full." Oak leaves dump every fall and pack into corners. Sweet gum balls wedge into downspout openings like they were designed for it.</p>

<p>We cleaned a house on Hustleville Road last month where the gutters looked "maybe a little full" from the ground. Got up there and found 4 inches of compacted debris that had basically turned to soil — earthworms and everything. The downspouts were packed solid. Nothing had drained properly in at least a year.</p>

<p>Clogged gutters cause real damage. Water overflows against the foundation. Fascia boards stay wet and rot. Landscaping erodes. The slow drip works its way behind siding. All of it costs more to fix than a cleaning would have cost to prevent.</p>

<p>A lot of folks try to clean their own gutters. We get it — it seems simple enough. But it's not fun work, it's genuinely dangerous (especially on two-stories), and unless you flush the downspouts properly, you're just moving the clog somewhere less visible.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Here's what we actually do, not just what the brochure says:</p>

<p><strong>Hand removal of debris.</strong> We scoop out everything by hand into buckets — not blow it onto your roof or lawn. Takes longer but does a better job.</p>

<p><strong>Downspout flush.</strong> Every downspout gets water run through it from a hose. If it's slow, we clear it. If it's blocked, we find out where and fix it. This is the step DIY cleaners skip, and it's why their gutters "clog up again right away."</p>

<p><strong>System inspection.</strong> While we're up there, we check hangers, seams, end caps, and the fascia behind the gutters. We're looking for loose hangers, cracks in the aluminum, gaps at seams, and soft spots in the wood. Takes an extra 10 minutes but catches problems early.</p>

<p><strong>Ground cleanup.</strong> Whatever fell while we were working gets cleaned up. We bag debris and take it with us.</p>

<p>The whole job takes 1-2 hours for most Albertville homes. You don't need to be there — just make sure we can access all sides of the house.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been cleaning gutters in Marshall County for over 20 years. We show up when we say, do thorough work, and charge fair prices. If we find a problem, we tell you straight — what it is, what it costs to fix, whether it's urgent or can wait.</p>

